**Structural note:** The config architecture has evolved significantly from what the CHECK spec assumes. Key differences:
- No standalone `config.yaml` — config is embedded in `.state/workflows.yaml` under `configs.mas-self`
- Tier system uses semantic token descriptions, not model-specific max_tokens/context_window
- No `providers:` section, `canonical_modes:`, `dispatch_control:`, `graceful_degradation:`, or `adaptive_tier_gate:` sections
- Agent registration happens in `sub_agents` categories (not `conflict_resolver.MAS-Sub-Agent_priority_order`)
- No lane segmentation (`routing_segmentation.lanes`) — agents categorized by function instead

